# SH-BLOCKED KNOWN GAP (Round XXXII Track D+E output-review B1, 2026-08-06):
# the `with v:` block requires SH's shared machinery. SH silently falls
# non-scalar `shared T` through to plain var-decl (the reverted `< PRIM_COUNT`
# gate at `tests/fixtures/self_host_lowerer/lower_stmt.gg:62-66`), so the SH
# lane DRIVER-FAILs on runtime_diff.
#
# ⚠ THE RUST CLASS-FIX IS PROVEN: this fixture passes on BOTH Rust backends
# (C + LLVM) — the integration test `shared_vector_ctor_init` (`#[ignore]`d,
# but the `run_gg` path asserts the intended `1` on the C backend). Its SH-lane
# blockage is what forces it into `known_gaps/` (out of runtime_diff auto-scan).
# Un-ignore + move back to `tests/fixtures/` once the SH `op_consume`
# non-scalar-inner follow-up (TODO.md) lands.
#
# Cell: ArcMutex · Vector[int] · ctor · no-spawn · pre-fix ICE 101 · post-fix `1`
#
# Part of the shared-var-decl class-fix fixture net (Core #11/#12). The
# push/len happen inside a bare `with v:` block — the shape that pins the
# writer-side class-fix's Move-follow-through WITHOUT tripping the fragile
# `for x in v:` iterator-invalidation shape (which pre-fix was green for the
# WRONG reason: downstream BB reshaping moved the violation out of the
# offending BB — Track E scout §"Corpus audit").

async void main():
    shared Vector[int] v = Vector[int]()
    with v:
        v.push(1)
        print(v.len())
